{
  "capture": "telemetry/mg90-d__dev-v006-2A-D/inductance/locked-4, telemetry/mg90-d__dev-v006-2A-D/inductance/wound-5, telemetry/mg90-d__dev-v006-2A-D/inductance/stop-6",
  "notes": "stage 3 inductance of mg90-d on dev-v006-2A-D: duty-step bursts into the held horn on a 5 V rail at three seats, inductance/locked-4 (the horn lock at mid travel, sitting 4), inductance/wound-5 (the same lock after a 24 % 300 ms reverse press, sitting 5) and inductance/stop-6 (the low end stop after the same press, sitting 6); at each, five groups in the order g1 25 % forward (the first after the seat was set, also after a reverse), g2 40 % forward, g3 40 % reverse, g4 25 % reverse, five bursts each, and g5 25 % reverse, three bursts after a 20 s rest. One burst is set aside by the rule that a burst reading a different current from its group from its first period on, at the same applied volts, reads a different circuit: stop-6/g1-fwd-25 burst 4 (first window current 19 % over its group's others); it stays in the edge pools, the fits table, its group's references and the length scan, and is out of every seat number and every key below but the stop_moving_burst_* keys. Estimators are stage 2 inductance's: the winding current per period is the window line at the middle of the bridge's window over the burst's own pre-step zero, nothing more taken off; the applied volts the two-part period mean of the tap difference with the edge correction pooled per seat, duty and sign; R and L by least squares of L (i[n+1] - i[n]) = T (V[n] - R (i[n] + i[n+1]) / 2) over the burst's period pairs, divided by sample-timing's window_scale k. l_ripple_mh is (V_on - R i) over the window's slope with R = r_locked_lap_100_ohm, the median of the last three periods, l_ripple_first_mh of the first three; early_* is the fit over the first three pairs; l_mh_r_pinned_by_duty is L with R pinned at r_locked_lap_100_ohm. The headline seat is the lock: l_mh, tau_us, r_burst_ohm, l_ripple_mh, l_ripple_first_mh, early_l_mh and early_r_ohm pool both duties (two populations, stage 2's form), *_by_duty carry each duty, the value the median over the lock's bursts after the first of each group and the bounds the range of its five group medians; r_burst_ohm is the end of the fit's slide, not the winding's resistance. applied_volts_drop_pct is the last period's volts over the first's, the lock's median with the three seats' medians as bounds; captures counts the held bursts after the first over the three seats; *_first_capture and *_other_captures are the lock's first bursts and the others with their full range; *_by_duty_sign the lock's medians; *_first_jump_pct_by_change and leftover_flux_uvs_by_change are the lock's first burst of each group over the median of its others and its volt-seconds beyond the others' R and L, one group per change, no bounds (the change keys name this stage's changes, g1 the seat set and a reversal); leftover_per_amp_uvs_per_a is g3's leftover over the g2 and g3 others' last window currents added, the lock with the two locks as bounds; l_slide_pct_by_duty and r_slide_pct_by_duty the fit's move from 3 to 8 pairs, the lock with the three seats as bounds; ripple_over_fit the ripple L over the fit, the two signs' medians averaged, the lock's group range; ripple_over_fit_inductors bridge-states' three inductive wirings, quoted; l_ripple_vs_current_mh_per_a the line of the window's L on its current over periods 1 and later at the lock, se bounds, the time trend and not a current dependence; l_of_i_l1_mh_per_a_by_duty the lock's L1 in L = L0 + L1 i over all pairs; v0_three_term_v the lock's constant drop as a third term over both duties, the two signs' mean with both as bounds, the wrong sign for a contact. crest_sample_less_window_mean_ma the window line at the crest shunt sample's instant (+31 ticks) less the line at the window middle (+27), median and 16-84 % over every held period of the three seats. g_hold_bound_ms is the held loss conductance the stage 3 sag stop laps allow (13 laps, 0.330 A, 4.344 ohm, rail slope -0.0055 +/- 0.0071 ohm/V, read from the sag result file), the slope over -R/I, +/- 2 sigma, a likely bound from one sitting; crest_less_mean_stop_lap_ma the crest's excess over the mean at the resistance stop chain's 24 and 36 % on 5 V (V_on 4.85 V) under that held bound, G (1 - D) V_on, the lower bound no correction and the upper the bound's +2 sigma, the systematic the resistance notebook carries; type_g_locked_ms (motor-model's fast locked-burst fit), type_g_spin_ms (spinning) and type_term_a_per_v (bemf-coast's meter term) are mg90-b's, carried for comparison only. r_locked_lap_100_ohm is the anchor, rest-resistance's read (V/I at the drive's first row from a line over 60 ms to the end) on resistance/locked-4's six 3.7 V laps, the mean with their range, this notebook's reading of those laps and the resistance notebook's to confirm (the 3.3 V laps sit off stage 1's graded lines). *_by_seat are each seat's median over its held bursts after the first per duty, bounds 16-84 % of a 4000-draw bootstrap over bursts (seed 0); seat_diff_pct_by_pair the second seat over the first in %, +/- one bootstrap sigma of the bursts' scatter only (the commutator angle's spread, about 8 % on L on the type, is not in it); first_jump_pct_by_seat_and_change the first-burst jumps and leftover at every seat; stop_forward_walk_uvs each held burst's leftover in the stop's two forward groups, the walk through the play, likely. stop_moving_burst_r_ohm, _l_ripple_mh and _i_first_ma are the burst set aside, a brush bridging two segments the leading reading, moderate. seat_pos_* are pot counts: the lock's seats.csv median with the burst metas' range; the wound lock's reading before the press, after it (with the burst metas' range) and after the groups; the stop's, blind on the pot's ADC rail; lock_span_sittings_4_5_counts the span of every manifest probe of sittings 4 and 5 and lock_probe_pos_sittings_4_5_counts their median and range, two seatings plus the lock's give; board_ntc_c the board NTC's median per sitting by the board's beta. Candidates: the reversal jump's size over the type's, the duty-up g2 jump, the ripple-over-fit gap 3 to 5 points under the type's, the wound lock's extra g1 leftover. Left out against stage 2's file: reversal_*, steps_*, fast_*, *_by_hole, even_over_odd_*, travel_bound_*, drive_offset_twice_pct, the bridge-states-k keys and leftover_rotor_angle_mrad_by_change (no such runs here, no holes, no mg90-d Ke result).",
